"""Run a portfolio of pono configurations on a model.

A portfolio is a YAML file that lists configurations of pono for each logic.
This script reads the logic of the model from its set-logic command and runs
the configurations listed for that logic in their order, a few at a time, each
in a process of its own that has limits on its CPU time and memory. The first
configuration that answers sat or unsat gives the answer: the script stops the
others and prints the output of that configuration.

Because a configuration fails alone when it exceeds its memory limit, a limit
on the memory of the whole run, such as the one that BenchExec enforces in
SV-COMP, does not end the run as long as the configurations that run at the
same time fit in it together: the script goes on with the next configuration.

The last configuration of a list can be a fallback, which starts only once
every other configuration of the list has ended without an answer, so that it
takes no CPU time from them, but uses what is left when they fail early. As
nothing waits for it, it has no CPU time limit.
"""

